      "sentences": [
        {
          "sid": "time-t1-s01",
          "c": "今日係星期一。",
          "j": "gam1 jat6 hai6 sing1 kei4 jat1.",
          "e": "Today is Monday.",
          "note": "Days of the week are simply numbered: 星期一 (sing1 kei4 jat1) \"week-one\" = Monday, through 星期六 (sing1 kei4 luk6) \"week-six\" = Saturday. The exception is Sunday — 星期日 (sing1 kei4 jat6) \"week-sun\", not \"week-seven\". Learn the numbers and six of seven days come free.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "今日",
              "j": "gam1 jat6",
              "e": "today"
            },
            {
              "c": "係",
              "j": "hai6",
              "e": "is"
            },
            {
              "c": "星期一",
              "j": "sing1 kei4 jat1",
              "e": "Monday"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "time-t1-s02",
          "c": "琴日係星期六。",
          "j": "kam4 jat6 hai6 sing1 kei4 luk6.",
          "e": "Yesterday was Saturday.",
          "note": "The everyday day-trio: 今日 (gam1 jat6) \"today\", 琴日 (kam4 jat6) \"yesterday\", 聽日 (ting1 jat6) \"tomorrow\". Cantonese also puts the time word first in the sentence, before the action.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "琴日",
              "j": "kam4 jat6",
              "e": "yesterday"
            },
            {
              "c": "係",
              "j": "hai6",
              "e": "was"
            },
            {
              "c": "星期六",
              "j": "sing1 kei4 luk6",
              "e": "Saturday"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "time-t1-s03",
          "c": "聽日朝早見。",
          "j": "ting1 jat6 ziu1 zou2 gin3.",
          "e": "See you tomorrow morning.",
          "note": "聽日 (ting1 jat6) is \"tomorrow\" and 朝早 (ziu1 zou2) is \"(in the) morning\" — stacked at the front as \"tomorrow morning\". 見 (gin3) \"see / meet\" on its own can mean \"see you\", with the subject left unsaid.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "聽日",
              "j": "ting1 jat6",
              "e": "tomorrow"
            },
            {
              "c": "朝早",
              "j": "ziu1 zou2",
              "e": "morning"
            },
            {
              "c": "見",
              "j": "gin3",
              "e": "see / meet"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "time-t1-s04",
          "c": "夜晚十點瞓覺。",
          "j": "je6 maan5 sap6 dim2 fan3 gaau3.",
          "e": "Sleep at 10pm.",
          "note": "點 (dim2) is \"o'clock\" — 十點 (sap6 dim2) \"ten o'clock\", and 幾點？(gei2 dim2?) asks \"what time?\". 夜晚 (je6 maan5) is \"night / evening\". 瞓覺 (fan3 gaau3) \"to sleep\" is distinctively Cantonese (not the Mandarin word).",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "夜晚",
              "j": "je6 maan5",
              "e": "night"
            },
            {
              "c": "十點",
              "j": "sap6 dim2",
              "e": "10 o'clock"
            },
            {
              "c": "瞓覺",
              "j": "fan3 gaau3",
              "e": "to sleep"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "time-t1-s05",
          "c": "星期日休息。",
          "j": "sing1 kei4 jat6 jau1 sik1.",
          "e": "Sunday is for resting.",
          "note": "星期日 (sing1 kei4 jat6) \"Sunday\" — the one day that breaks the numbering (see Monday's note). 休息 (jau1 sik1) is the everyday word for \"rest / take a break / have time off\".",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "星期日",
              "j": "sing1 kei4 jat6",
              "e": "Sunday"
            },
            {
              "c": "休息",
              "j": "jau1 sik1",
              "e": "to rest"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "time-t1-s06",
          "c": "我生日係三月十號。",
          "j": "ngo5 saang1 jat6 hai6 saam1 jyut6 sap6 hou6.",
          "e": "My birthday is the 10th of March.",
          "note": "月 (jyut6) \"month\" and <b>號</b> (hou6) \"date / day of month\" are the building blocks of dates: 三月十號 (saam1 jyut6 sap6 hou6) = \"March 10th\". 幾月幾號 (gei2 jyut6 gei2 hou6) = \"what date?\"",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "我",
              "j": "ngo5",
              "e": "I"
            },
            {
              "c": "生日",
              "j": "saang1 jat6",
              "e": "birthday"
            },
            {
              "c": "係",
              "j": "hai6",
              "e": "is"
            },
            {
              "c": "三月",
              "j": "saam1 jyut6",
              "e": "March"
            },
            {
              "c": "十號",
              "j": "sap6 hou6",
              "e": "10th"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "time-t1-s07",
          "c": "今年係我第一年學廣東話。",
          "j": "gam1 nin4 hai6 ngo5 dai6 jat1 nin4 hok6 gwong2 dung1 waa2.",
          "e": "This year is my first year learning Cantonese.",
          "note": "年 (nin4) \"year\" follows the same logic: 今年 (gam1 nin4) \"this year\", 去年 (heoi3 nin4) \"last year\" (not in the word list but useful), 明年 (ming4 nin4) \"next year\". Numbers + 年 give the calendar year.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "今年",
              "j": "gam1 nin4",
              "e": "this year"
            },
            {
              "c": "係",
              "j": "hai6",
              "e": "is"
            },
            {
              "c": "我",
              "j": "ngo5",
              "e": "my"
            },
            {
              "c": "第一年",
              "j": "dai6 jat1 nin4",
              "e": "first year"
            },
            {
              "c": "學廣東話",
              "j": "hok6 gwong2 dung1 waa2",
              "e": "learning Cantonese"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "time-t1-s08",
          "c": "上個月好忙，下個月應該好啲。",
          "j": "soeng6 go3 jyut6 hou2 mong4, haa6 go3 jyut6 jing1 goi1 hou2 di1.",
          "e": "Last month was hectic — next month should be better.",
          "note": "上個月 (soeng6 go3 jyut6) \"last month\" and <b>下個月</b> (haa6 go3 jyut6) \"next month\" follow the same 上/下 (soeng6/haa6) \"above/below\" logic as 上個星期/下個星期 (last/next week). A consistent Cantonese pattern.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "上個月",
              "j": "soeng6 go3 jyut6",
              "e": "last month"
            },
            {
              "c": "好忙",
              "j": "hou2 mong4",
              "e": "very busy"
            },
            {
              "c": "下個月",
              "j": "haa6 go3 jyut6",
              "e": "next month"
            },
            {
              "c": "應該",
              "j": "jing1 goi1",
              "e": "should"
            },
            {
              "c": "好啲",
              "j": "hou2 di1",
              "e": "better"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
